<title>FRANCE: Flights into Paris delayed by NATO air exercise.</title>
<headline>Flights into Paris delayed by NATO air exercise.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Evening flights into Paris's Charles de Gaulle airport, mostly from other European countries, were suffering delays of about an hour due to a major NATO exercise on Wednesday, civil aviation authorities said.</p>
<p>Delays were expected to continue until Friday. Some 350 combat aircraft from North Atlantic Treaty Organisation countries are taking part in the manoeuvre which began on Tuesday and ends on Friday, the officials told reporters.</p>
</text>
